/** Ben's Food Court - Ben's Burritos' food in 3D (docs/api/food.md section 12 walks through it; docs/api/packs/burrito.md
 *  section 10 is the list of looks it draws).
 *
 *  The same toon style as the Burger Bar and the Pizza Parlor: chunky cel-shaded food with ink outlines. Nothing here
 *  stacks, so the kit's `stack` is never used. Every filling lies ON what is under it: a layout keeps a "ground" (the
 *  height of the food at any point) and gives each part a region of it (a band down a tortilla, a strip in a taco, a
 *  wedge or a heap in a bowl); a part builds its mound or its pieces on that ground and raises it for the next part, so
 *  nothing floats and nothing sinks (food.md 7: bounding boxes are not surfaces).
 *
 *    burrito       the flat flour tortilla on its square of foil, the fillings in a band down its middle in line order
 *                  and the hot sauce zigzagged over them; once wrapped (made.auto has `wrap`), a fat rolled burrito
 *                  lying across the counter, its closed end in foil, the open end cut on the bias toward the viewer
 *                  showing the fillings' colours; once burst (`burst`), the same in a second tortilla (two tortilla
 *                  edges at the open end), with beans, rice and a smear of sour cream spilled on a scrap of foil
 *    bowl          the orange bowl with its green rim stripe: rice and beans in the bottom and the rest in loose heaps;
 *                  once arranged (`arrange`), every part its own tidy wedge, nothing touching, the sauce across
 *    tacos         three small soft tortillas on a steel holder tray, open with the fillings in a strip; once folded
 *                  (`fold`), three half-moons standing in the holder's V rods, the fillings showing along the top
 *    chipsBasket   a red-and-white checked paper boat of tortilla chips, the salsa cup and the guacamole cup beside it,
 *                  the lime wedge on the rim
 *    giantBurrito  the burrito, drawn 1.6x by the kit, with a red pennant with a flame stuck in its top
 *
 *  The vessel drawn is the style PICKED (made.picks.style): a bowl picked for a burrito ticket is drawn as a bowl.
 *  The toast is a `want`: read from made.picks.toast (o.stage on the griddle). Doneness is a colour AND a mark
 *  (DESIGN.md): the tortilla browns through the pack's ramp and gets press stripes, 0 / 2 faint / 3 brown with toasty
 *  spots / 4 dark with blistered crisp edges / black with smoke.
 *
 *  Sets, by backdrop name: counter (spec 5.2: line 0.80, a cream top with the storefront's orange plank edge), prep
 *  (the painted steel counter is the surface: the burrito line and the chip basket) and griddle (the painted dark
